Xenia
https://github.com/xenia-project/xenia
Reference commit: 95a5c3ee250f80c3b9d139658649d9ffb6db3eec
Copyright (c) 2015, Ben Vanik and contributors
License: BSD-3-Clause

Copied files:
  runtime/kernel/nt_status_table.inc   NT status -> Win32 error tables
                                       copied from
                                       src/xenia/kernel/xboxkrnl/xboxkrnl_error.cc
                                       (Copyright 2022 Ben Vanik; only change:
                                       xe::countof -> std::size)

Vendored GPU code: thirdparty/xenia/ contains files of xenia-canary
(https://github.com/xenia-canary/xenia-canary, commit
e6cd2e4bc998609ca25e24a24c8e32b66c5908ad) copied without manual changes by
the tools/vendor_xenia.py script, with the original headers intact; the only
changes are the patches in thirdparty/xenia/patches/ (every hunk marked
"gow2:"). List of the files, of the patches with their reason and of the
shims in thirdparty/xenia/VENDORED.md; license in thirdparty/xenia/LICENSE
(same text as below). The shims in runtime/gpu/shims/ reproduce Xenia
interfaces (include paths, names, signatures) with implementations of this
project and cite in their header the Xenia file they replace. The presenter
(runtime/gpu/presenter.cpp) uses two precompiled DXBC shaders of Xenia, also
in thirdparty/xenia/
(src/xenia/ui/shaders/bytecode/d3d12_5_1/guest_output_bilinear_ps.h and
guest_output_triangle_strip_rect_vs.h), under the same license; the two
sharpening shaders (guest_output_ffx_cas_sharpen_ps.h,
guest_output_ffx_cas_resample_ps.h) derive from AMD FidelityFX CAS
(Copyright (c) Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., MIT license). The APU (XMA
decoding: src/xenia/apu/xma_context*, xma_register_*, base/bit_stream) is
also in thirdparty/xenia/, at the same xenia-canary commit, with patches 0007
and 0008.

Also used as the reference for the semantics of the Xbox 360 kernel
functions; the adapted parts cite in a comment the reference Xenia function
(src/xenia/kernel/xboxkrnl/*.cc, src/xenia/kernel/xam/*.cc, xthread.cc,
xobject.cc, util/object_table.cc; for the fake GPU in runtime/gpu_fake/:
src/xenia/gpu/graphics_system.cc, command_processor.cc, xenos.h). Files with
these references: runtime/kernel/*.cpp, runtime/kernel/io/*.cpp,
runtime/gpu_fake/*.cpp.

