Copyright (c) the FFmpeg developers
License: GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later (LGPL-2.1-or-later)

Subset of libavcodec and libavutil with the xenia-canary decoders
(xmaframes, the only one used, plus mp3 and wma), vendored in
thirdparty/ffmpeg/ by the tools/vendor_ffmpeg.py script with the original
headers intact; compiled into the xenia_ffmpeg static library and
incorporated into this project's GPL-3.0 binary under section 3 of the
LGPL-2.1 (the LGPL allows applying the terms of the GPL to the files). The
complete source of the subset is in thirdparty/ffmpeg/; license text in
thirdparty/ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1, project note in
thirdparty/ffmpeg/LICENSE.md. List of the files with their origin and
license, patches with reason and date (none at the moment) in
thirdparty/ffmpeg/VENDORED.md. No file of the subset is under the GPL (no
CONFIG_GPL or CONFIG_NONFREE enabled; libavutil/macos_kperf.h, GPL and
macOS-only, is excluded).

Some files of the subset have their own permissive license, stated in their
header: libavcodec/faandct.c (ISC), libavutil/adler32.c (zlib),
libavutil/avsscanf.c (MIT, from musl), libavcodec/jfdctfst.c,
libavcodec/jfdctint_template.c, libavcodec/jrevdct.c (IJG license): this
software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

